# What `await` hands back comes in the register of results, which is also that of first arguments. Where it is no number, which is rare, it is the second argument of a call:
# it is read there before the first argument is written, so it stays in its register on the way that is taken, and nothing stands between the call and the test of its result.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="mix" role=CoroutineBody
# CHECK: Successors: Rare:#{{*}}, #[[second]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[second]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors:
# CHECK-NEXT: Move
# CHECK-NEXT: Patch
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch64 Below,
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Rare:#{{*}}, #[[mixes]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[mixes]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors:
# CHECK-NEXT: Move
# CHECK-NEXT: Xor32
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
